{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/abxzk1","slideIndex":1,"text":"0:40. Users register and sign in, then start a GPS session on the map. The map shows neighborhood boundaries and ownership colors. A runner who beats a neighborhood step record can claim that turf. The leaderboard shows the current owner and record, and the profile summarizes personal activity. Friends, neighborhood chat, trophies and notifications support the competitive loop. The current evidence is from the iOS simulator in a single supported city.\nPhoto: AI-generated illustration of a runner checking a sports watch."}
