{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/ntbg6s","slideIndex":2,"text":"0:50. On the left is the React Native client. It gets location updates and includes the Timișoara neighborhood polygons. The client uses an HTTP REST API running locally in this development setup. Express handles authentication, sessions, ownership, and social data. It connects over TLS to PostgreSQL on Render. Passwords are hashed with bcrypt, and authenticated requests use JWTs. The client polls for map and neighborhood chat updates. The client-to-API and API-to-database connections have different transports."}
