{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/408nzx","slideIndex":4,"text":"0:55. On the map, Start Tracking opens an activity session. Location updates record points and let the server estimate distance and steps using a 0.7-meter stride. A point is matched to a neighborhood polygon, and the session accumulates estimated steps in that neighborhood. When the session beats the stored record, the neighborhood changes hands. The leaderboard shows Fabric at 10,036 steps for User4 in the seeded demo.\nScreenshots: User1 on the iPhone 17e simulator, map.png."}
